<h2>Cookie Dough Blizzard Cake — Serving and Storage Tips</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Remove from freezer 5–10 minutes before cutting</strong> — DQ Cakes slice cleanest at a slight thaw. Straight-from-freezer hard cuts can crack the layers unevenly.</li>
<li><strong>Use a warm knife</strong> — Run a sharp knife under warm water and dry it before each cut for clean, professional-looking slices.</li>
<li><strong>Store leftovers tightly wrapped</strong> — If you have leftover cake, cover the exposed cut edges with plastic wrap before returning to the freezer. The cookie dough pieces harden more than soft serve if left exposed.</li>
<li><strong>Pair with the individual Blizzard</strong> — For guests who want more, the <a href="/items/cookie-dough-blizzard">Cookie Dough Blizzard</a> (from $3.49) alongside a slice creates the ultimate cookie dough DQ experience.</li>
</ul>
